# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
build/
dist/
.venv/

# Heavy run corpora + model artifacts (regenerated on the cluster; see docs/DATA.md)
reports/
*.npz

# Figure data (`make figdata`) IS COMMITTED — do not ignore it.
#
# The plotters read figdata/figNN_*.json and nothing else: no reports/, no model
# corpus, no jax.  Committing it (~136 kB for all nine) is what makes the claim in
# registry.py, figures/README.md and docs/DATA.md true — that every figure rebuilds
# from a bare clone with only matplotlib.  Recomputing it instead needs the
# multi-GB corpora and the cluster, which a reader or a co-author cloning the repo
# does not have.
#
# This previously read `paper/figures/figdata/*.json` with a note that fig08/fig09
# would be force-added as a fallback.  That force-add never happened, so figdata
# was never committed at all and `figNN_*_plot.py` could not run from a clone.

# Throwaway layout renders (see paper/figures/mockups/README.md). Placeholder panels
# live here, so nothing in this directory may ever be mistaken for a paper figure.
paper/figures/mockups/

# Table build outputs (recomputed by `make tabdata`). The rendered tab??_*.tex ARE
# committed, so `pdflatex` always works — as the figure PDFs are.
paper/tables/tabdata/*.json

# LaTeX build artifacts
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log
paper/*.fls
paper/*.fdb_latexmk
paper/*.synctex.gz
paper/*.out
paper/*.blg

# OS / editor
.DS_Store

# Cloud-sync conflicted-copy artifacts (never commit these)
* [0-9].*

# SLURM job logs (created at submit time)
logs/
